-- The evidence for NOTES.md section 4, Findings: each assertion shows a surprising answer the
-- wording gives, and is EXPECTED TO BE SATISFIED. The finding numbers are NOTES.md's.
-- Expected values are worked from the source, as in lpa-tests.l4; scenario figures (limits,
-- dates) are hypothetical.

§ `Findings`

§§ `Fixtures`

`Minh` MEANS `An insured person` WITH
    `date of birth`                                                         IS YMD 1990 5 15
    `place in the group`                                                    IS `an employee of the employer`
    `a Vietnamese citizen`                                                  IS TRUE
    `living in Vietnam when cover began, as declared in the application`    IS TRUE
    `living in Vietnam on a tourist visa`                                   IS FALSE
    `a citizen of a country under United Nations, United States, European Union or United Kingdom sanctions` IS FALSE
    `occupation class`                                                      IS `class 1`
    `left-handed`                                                           IS JUST FALSE
    `degree of permanent disability before the effective date`              IS 0
    `insured under the same contract as a parent, adoptive parent or legal guardian` IS FALSE
    `in full-time study, with a valid student card or proof of it`          IS FALSE
    `keeps a valid visa or temporary residence card`                        IS TRUE

GIVEN `the death limit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the injury limit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The policy schedule`
`a 2026 schedule, death limit` `the death limit` `, injury limit` `the injury limit` MEANS
    `The policy schedule` WITH
        `first day of the period of insurance`  IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `last day of the period of insurance`   IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `a renewal`                             IS FALSE
        `worldwide geographical scope`          IS TRUE
        `death limit`                           IS `the death limit`
        `permanent injury limit`                IS `the injury limit`
        `temporary injury benefit`              IS NOTHING
        `medical expense limit`                 IS JUST 50000000
        `daily hospital allowance`              IS JUST 400000
        `food poisoning cover agreed`           IS FALSE

`the findings schedule` MEANS `a 2026 schedule, death limit` (JUST 1000000000) `, injury limit` (JUST 1000000000)

GIVEN `absences` IS A LIST OF `An absence from Vietnam`
      `changes`  IS A LIST OF `A change increasing the risk`
GIVETH A `The insured's cover facts`
`cover facts with absences` `absences` `and changes` `changes` MEANS
    `The insured's cover facts` WITH
        `date of entry into Vietnam, if after the first day of the period`      IS NOTHING
        `date the insured became eligible, if after the first day of the period` IS NOTHING
        `date the insured ceased to be eligible, for a reason other than age`   IS NOTHING
        `date the group contract ended`                                         IS NOTHING
        `date employment with the employer ended`                               IS NOTHING
        `date membership of the sponsoring organisation ended`                  IS NOTHING
        `date the insured member's own cover ended`                             IS NOTHING
        `date the benefits were used up`                                        IS NOTHING
        `premium for the insured paid in full within the payment period`        IS TRUE
        `last day of the payment period`                                        IS YMD 2026 1 31
        `absences from Vietnam`                                                 IS `absences`
        `changes increasing the risk`                                           IS `changes`

§§ `D1. "hoặc đang thực hiện công việc": general exclusion 6(d) read literally excludes every injury at work`

-- An office worker injured at work: the encoding's reading (fork F22) engages no exclusion;
-- the literal reading of 6(d) excludes it, in a policy bought to insure employees.
#ASSERT `the exclusions engaged by` `performing work` `under` `the findings schedule` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `general exclusion 6(d) read literally excludes` `performing work`

§§ `D2. Cover ends retroactively on the day the insured LEFT Vietnam (7.1(e))`

-- An insured who leaves on 1 March 2026 without notice and is injured abroad on 1 April: on
-- the facts as they stand after 180 days, cover is not in force on 1 April; had the insured
-- come home on day 180, it would have been.
#ASSERT NOT `the insured's cover was in force on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, for` `Minh` `under` `the findings schedule` `and` (`cover facts with absences` (LIST `An absence from Vietnam` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), 181, FALSE, FALSE) `and changes` EMPTY)
#ASSERT     `the insured's cover was in force on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, for` `Minh` `under` `the findings schedule` `and` (`cover facts with absences` (LIST `An absence from Vietnam` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), 180, FALSE, FALSE) `and changes` EMPTY)
-- And 3(f) allows only 180 days abroad at a time under worldwide cover, whatever the notice.
#ASSERT NOT `general provision 3(f): a stay abroad is within the limit, under` `the findings schedule` `, lasting` 181

§§ `D3. An unpaid premium: 16B(b) pays 0,1%, 4(b) pays nothing; on a hospital allowance 0,1% is 400 đồng`

-- 4(b): no liability arises if a condition precedent (premium, 4(a)(ii)) is not met.
-- 16B(b): for an event before the automatic termination, at most 0,1% of the limit.
#ASSERT `general provision 16B(b): the most paid on a claim, the programme limit being` 1000000000 `and the summary limit` 1000000000 EQUALS 1000000
#ASSERT `general provision 16B(b): the most paid on a claim, the programme limit being` 400000 `and the summary limit` 400000 EQUALS 400

§§ `D4. Limitation 1(b): the top-up for death after a permanent injury benefit can almost never be paid`

-- Partial permanence exists only from 52 weeks after the accident (10 January 2026 + 364 =
-- 9 January 2027). The top-up needs death within 52 weeks of the Injury: by the same day. A
-- death one day later, after 400.000.000 was paid for the lost eye, adds nothing; the same
-- death with no permanent injury claim pays the whole 1.000.000.000 (within 24 months).
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 1 10) PLUS `the days in 52 weeks` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 9
#ASSERT `limitation 1(b): the death benefit payable, given` 1000000000 `and a permanent injury benefit of` 400000000 `paid for an injury on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, death on` (YMD 2027 1 10) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `limitation 1(b): the death benefit payable, given` 1000000000 `and a permanent injury benefit of` 0 `paid for an injury on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, death on` (YMD 2027 1 10) EQUALS 1000000000
#ASSERT `death within 24 months of the accident:` (YMD 2026 1 10) `and` (YMD 2027 1 10)

§§ `D5. General provision 13: deadlines that cannot all be met`

-- (i) If "sự kiện bảo hiểm" is the accident, the one-year limit ends long before a total
-- permanent injury can exist (104 weeks).
#ASSERT `add years` (YMD 2026 1 10) 1 LESS THAN ((YMD 2026 1 10) PLUS `the days in 104 weeks`)
-- (ii) The forms and evidence are due within 30 days of the insured event, and 13(d) voids a
-- claim out of time: a claim file sent on day 200, well within the year, fails if the forms
-- go with it. The one-year period of 13(a) (and of Law 08/2022/QH15 art 30) does no work.
#ASSERT NOT `done, if at all, by` ((YMD 2026 3 10) PLUS 30) `: on` (JUST ((YMD 2026 3 10) PLUS 200))
#ASSERT     `done, if at all, by` (`add years` (YMD 2026 3 10) 1) `: on` (JUST ((YMD 2026 3 10) PLUS 200))

§§ `D6. The teeth bands`

-- Exactly 8 teeth, or more than 8 that dentures can replace: no band. 3 teeth: two bands.
#ASSERT `the row for the loss of` 8 `teeth, replaceable by dentures:` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the row for the loss of` 12 `teeth, replaceable by dentures:` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the rate printed for` `loss of 3 to 4 teeth` EQUALS `one rate` (8%)
#ASSERT `the rate printed for` `loss of 1 to 3 teeth` EQUALS `one rate` (3%)
-- The 1-3 teeth row (3%) is under the 5% rule, so on its own it never pays.
#ASSERT `benefit A.2, the rate payable, for the accident on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `and the assessment` (`The permanent injury claim` OF (YMD 2027 1 9), TRUE, TRUE, (LIST `A claimed permanent injury` OF (`loss of teeth` 3 TRUE), FALSE)) `, left-handedness` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS 8%
#ASSERT `benefit A.2, the rate payable, for the accident on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `and the assessment` (`The permanent injury claim` OF (YMD 2027 1 9), TRUE, TRUE, (LIST `A claimed permanent injury` OF (`loss of teeth` 2 TRUE), FALSE)) `, left-handedness` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS 0

