#ASSERT count `every set of fingers` EQUALS 31
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN fs YIELD isNothing (`the row for the amputation of the fingers` fs)) `every set of fingers`) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT count `every set of toes` EQUALS 31
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN ts YIELD isNothing (`the row for the amputation of the toes` ts)) `every set of toes`) EQUALS 20
-- The 50% ankylosis rule for toes other than the big toe has no amputation amount to halve.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the rate for the permanent injury` (`ankylosis of the joints of toes of one foot` (LIST `the second toe`)) `, the insured's left-handedness being` (JUST FALSE) BECAUSE "the injury is not in the tables, and its rate is for the Company to decide by comparison"
-- Ankylosis of the non-dominant middle finger: 2,5%, under the 5% rule, never paid alone.
#ASSERT `the rate for the permanent injury` (`ankylosis of the joints of fingers of one hand` (LIST `the middle finger`) `the left side`) `, the insured's left-handedness being` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS 2.5%

§§ `D8. Three rules for medical expenses another contract also covers`

-- Bills of 10.000.000; another contract paid 4.000.000; this limit 50.000.000 of 100.000.000.
-- Limitation 4: the excess, 6.000.000. General provision 11: the excess, 6.000.000, OR the
-- rateable share, 5.000.000. Special exclusion 3: nothing.
#ASSERT `general provision 11: the excess of` 10000000 `over` 4000000 EQUALS 6000000
#ASSERT `general provision 11: the rateable share of` 10000000 `, this limit being` 50000000 `of total limits` 100000000 EQUALS 5000000

§§ `D9. 52 weeks or 12 months for medical expenses`

-- Accident 10 March 2026: 52 weeks end on 9 March 2027, 12 months on 10 March 2027. A bill of
-- 10 March 2027 is inside the definition (src 229) and outside benefit C's words (src 512).
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 3 10) PLUS `the days in 52 weeks` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 9
#ASSERT `benefit C, the amount allowed for the expense` (`A medical expense` OF `surgery`, 1000000, 1000000, YMD 2027 3 10, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) `after the accident on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS 1000000

§§ `D11. Special provision 5 against general exclusion 5(g)`

-- A sudden, accidental asphyxiation by toxic fumes: covered on the encoding's reading (F21),
-- although 5(g) excludes "hít phải hơi độc, khí độc, chất độc" without qualification.
#ASSERT `the exclusions engaged by` (`inhaling smoke, toxic vapour, gas or poison` TRUE FALSE) `under` `the findings schedule` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `D12. Any Injury must be notified "ngay" (7.1(f)), against 30 days (13(a))`

-- Read literally, the claimed injury of 10 March 2026, notified on day 20 (in time under
-- 13(a)) but not at once, ends cover on 10 March itself.
#ASSERT NOT `the insured's cover was in force on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, for` `Minh` `under` `the findings schedule` `and` (`cover facts with absences` EMPTY `and changes` (LIST `A change increasing the risk` OF (YMD 2026 3 10), FALSE))

§§ `D13. Limitation 1(c) rests on benefit A, which is optional`

-- A programme without benefit A: on the literal reading the cap on all benefits is 0.
#ASSERT `limitation 1(c) read literally: the cap, under` (`a 2026 schedule, death limit` NOTHING `, injury limit` NOTHING) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `limitation 1(c): the most all benefits pay one insured in the period, under` (`a 2026 schedule, death limit` NOTHING `, injury limit` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `D15. "Any race" (4(e)) swallows the carve-out for racing on foot (4(l))`

#ASSERT `the exclusions engaged by` `a race, or a test of speed or endurance` `under` `the findings schedule` EQUALS LIST `general exclusion 4(e), a race or a speed or endurance test`

§§ `D16. The short-period bands share their edges`

-- Exactly 3 months: "Đến 3 tháng" (40%) and "Từ 3 tháng đến 6 tháng" (70%) both apply. The
-- encoding takes 40% (fork F38).
#ASSERT `general provision 9: the short-period rate, cover from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS 40%
#ASSERT `general provision 9: the short-period rate, cover from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS 70%

§§ `D17. A 5 cm shortening is in two bands`

#ASSERT `the rate printed for` `shortening of a leg by at least about 5 cm` EQUALS `one rate` (30%)
#ASSERT `the rate printed for` `shortening of a leg by 3 to 5 cm` EQUALS `one rate` (20%)

§§ `D18. The application outranks the endorsements that amend the contract`

#ASSERT `general provision 1: the document that prevails between` `an endorsement` `and` `the application, quotation, renewal notice or renewal quotation` EQUALS `the application, quotation, renewal notice or renewal quotation`

§§ `D24. Property-insurance exclusions in an accident wording`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the exclusions engaged by` `property at a nuclear installation, nuclear fuel or material, or supplying such an installation` `under` `the findings schedule`

§§ `D28. A 30-day period has a payment period that ends after it`

-- "If the period is under 30 days" (16A(a)): a period of exactly 30 days (1-30 January) takes
-- the ordinary 30 days from the effective date, which end on 31 January (fork F35).
#ASSERT `general provision 16A: the last day of the payment period, effective` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, the period ending` (YMD 2026 1 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

§§ `D31. An extension that cuts cover: motorcycles over 150cc`

#ASSERT `special provision 8 is not met by` (`riding a motorcycle, as driver or passenger` 175)
